          "body": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **Legacy package fallback added**\n\nThe new `_evidence_failure_snapshot` wrapper explicitly supports older installed packages by returning `None` when their diagnostics module is missing. This violates the repository directive prohibiting legacy fallbacks and support. Require the current diagnostics contract here, retaining the existing outer diagnostic-error boundary so failures cannot replace the original probe exception. This repository requirement must be satisfied before merging.\n\n**Rule Used:** What: \"Legacy\" should not be supported  Why: We want to eliminate tech debt   Good: No legacy fallbacks, redirects, tests, etc. ([source](https://app.greptile.com/hol/-/custom-context?memory=c1ba7189-733a-40b9-8b0d-2e7a5f85a373))\n\nNote: If this suggestion doesn't match your team's coding style, reply to this and let me know. I'll remember it for next time!\n\n<a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/ide/codex?prompt=IMPORTANT%3A%20Work%20in%20the%20repository%20%22hashgraph-online%2Fhol-guard%22%20on%20the%20existing%20branch%20%22chore%2Fresolve-2797-conflicts%22.%20Checkout%20that%20branch%20%E2%80%94%20do%20NOT%20create%20a%20new%20branch%20or%20open%20a%20new%20PR.%20Push%20your%20changes%20to%20%22chore%2Fresolve-2797-conflicts%22.%0A%0AThis%20is%20a%20comment%20left%20during%20a%20code%20review.%0APath%3A%20ci%2Fnative_runtime%2Fdefault_auto_failure.py%0ALine%3A%20129-134%0A%0AComment%3A%0A**Legacy%20package%20fallback%20added**%0A%0AThe%20new%20%60_evidence_failure_snapshot%60%20wrapper%20explicitly%20supports%20older%20installed%20packages%20by%20returning%20%60None%60%20when%20their%20diagnostics%20module%20is%20missing.%20This%20violates%20the%20repository%20directive%20prohibiting%20legacy%20fallbacks%20and%20support.%20Require%20the%20current%20diagnostics%20contract%20here%2C%20retaining%20the%20existing%20outer%20diagnostic-error%20boundary%20so%20failures%20cannot%20replace%20the%20original%20probe%20exception.%20This%20repository%20requirement%20must%20be%20satisfied%20before%20merging.%0A%0A**Rule%20Used%3A**%20What%3A%20%22Legacy%22%20should%20not%20be%20supported%20%20Why%3A%20We%20want%20to%20eliminate%20tech%20debt%20%20%20Good%3A%20No%20legacy%20fallbacks%2C%20redirects%2C%20tests%2C%20etc.%20%28%5Bsource%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fapp.greptile.com%2Fhol%2F-%2Fcustom-context%3Fmemory%3Dc1ba7189-733a-40b9-8b0d-2e7a5f85a373%29%29%0A%0A---%0A%0AFor%20each%20issue%20above%2C%20determine%20whether%20it%20is%20valid%20and%20should%20be%20fixed.%20If%20so%2C%20fix%20it%20directly.&repo=hashgraph-online%2Fhol-guard&pr=2974&platform=github\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInCodexDark.svg?v=7\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInCodex.svg?v=7\"><img alt=\"Fix in Codex\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/FixInCodex.svg?v=7\"></picture></a>",
